      "id": "MJUe",
      "code_hash": "b29bbbb59b391e75982a7fae74db82b3",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"model-kinds\">Model kinds</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">This notebook puts the three kinds of EBM side by side: a binary classifier, a multiclass classifier and a\nregressor. You learn how EBaMl reads the kind of a model, what a score means for each kind, how the graph text\ndiffers, and which fields the local explanations give.</span>\n<ul>\n<li>You need no data download: the iris data comes with scikit-learn.</li>\n<li>Everything outside the buttons runs without a key and sends no request.</li>\n<li>The buttons at the end send real requests. The default model needs <code>OPENROUTER_API_KEY</code>. Pass <code>model=</code> to use\n  another model, as the documentation page \"Choosing the model\" shows.</li>\n</ul></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "vblA",
      "code_hash": "4cd7ad32d308c8709972b9dc72d6094b",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"three-ebms-on-the-same-features\">Three EBMs on the same features</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The three models read the same three features of the iris data. Only the target changes:</span>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Model</th>\n<th>Target</th>\n<th>Kind</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>binary</code></td>\n<td>Is the flower a virginica?</td>\n<td>Binary classifier</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>multiclass</code></td>\n<td>The species of the flower</td>\n<td>Multiclass classifier</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>regressor</code></td>\n<td>The petal width, in centimetres</td>\n<td>Regressor</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><code>model_kind</code> reads the kind of each fitted EBM from its link function. Each kind gives the names of the outputs\nand the meaning of a score.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "bkHC",
      "code_hash": "b62a06d56054e501b30a9ff866844b74",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
